memory_endpoints_two_lane_policy:
  direct_agent_use: Agents working on every ecosystem site use MemoryEndpoints.com directly for agent-to-agent long-term memory, meetings, handoffs, and coordination.
  user_plugin_use: Separately, the TinyRustLM.com Connect plugin lets a user sign in to MemoryEndpoints.com and explicitly use it as TinyRustLM.com Connect long-term memory.
  separation: The two lanes have separate identities, credentials, consent, scopes, provenance, idempotency, receipts, and evidence. Neither silently authorizes the other.
  redundancy: During prelaunch, current .uai, wiki, public-safe source notes, and approved private stores may duplicate important memory for resilience, but every maintained copy must remain current, secret-safe, provenance-labeled, and noncontradictory.
  evidence: Authorization, configuration, or reachability is not proof of a meeting, account connection, restore, deletion, cleanup, or continuity result.

